NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000765 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000766 "=head1 TODO"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000767 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000768 "=head2 Deferred plans"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000769 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000770 "Sometimes you don't know the number of tests you will run when you use"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000771 "C<Test::More>.  The C<plan()> function allows you to delay specifying the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000772 "plan, but you must still call it before the tests are run.  This is an error:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000773 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000774 " use Test::More;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000775 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000776 " my $tests = 0;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000777 " foreach my $test ("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000778 "     my $count = run($test); # assumes tests are being run"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000779 "     $tests += $count;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000780 " }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000781 " plan($tests);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000782 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000783 "The way around this is typically to use 'no_plan' and when the tests are done,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000784 "C<Test::Builder> merely sets the plan to the number of tests run.  We'd like"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000785 "for the programmer to specify this number instead of letting C<Test::Builder>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000786 "do it.  However, C<Test::Builder> internals are a bit difficult to work with,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000787 "so we're delaying this feature."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000788 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000789 "=head2 Cleaner skip()"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000790 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000791 " if ( $some_condition ) {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000792 "     skip $message, $num_tests;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000793 " }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000794 " else {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000795 "     # run those tests"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000796 " }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000797 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000798 "That would be cleaner and I might add it if enough people want it."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000799 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000800 "=head1 CAVEATS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000801 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000802 "Because of how Perl handles arguments, and because diagnostics are not really"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000803 "part of the Test Anything Protocol, what actually happens internally is that"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000804 "we note that a test has failed and we throw an exception or bail out as soon"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000805 "as the I<next> test is called (but before it runs).  This means that its"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000806 "arguments are automatically evaluated before we can take action:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000807 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000808 " use Test::Most qw<no_plan die>;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000809 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000810 " ok $foo, 'Die if this fails';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000811 " ok factorial(123456),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000812 "   '... but wait a loooong time before you throw an exception';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000813 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000814 "=head1 ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000815 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000816 "Many thanks to C<perl-qa> for arguing about this so much that I just went"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000817 "ahead and did it :)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000818 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000819 "Thanks to Aristotle for suggesting a better way to die or bailout."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000820 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000821 "Thanks to 'swillert' (L<http://use.perl.org/~swillert/>) for suggesting a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000822 "better implementation of my \"dumper explain\" idea"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000823 "(L<http://use.perl.org/~Ovid/journal/37004>)."
